  "body": "## What changed\n\n`camcraft_post::data_dir::cargo_profile_dir` (`crates/post/src/data_dir.rs`) now accepts the old and the new cargo build-dir layout.\n\n- Old layout (no change): the exe is in `target/<profile>` or in its `deps` / `examples` child. The profile folder holds `.fingerprint`.\n- New layout: a test exe is in `target/<profile>/build/<pkg>/<hash>/out`. The function maps it to `target/<profile>`. A profile folder that holds `build/camcraft-post` is a cargo build tree. This marker also applies to the uplifted binaries in `target/<profile>`.\n\nAn installed exe without its `assets/<kind>` folder is still refused by name. The decision is in `docs/decisions/2316-data-dir-new-layout.md`.\n\n## Readings (run 43990986558, `gate-logs` artifact)\n\n```\n     Running unittests src/lib.rs (target/debug/build/camcraft-post/4d4a6b2fbedf41a7/out/camcraft_post-4d4a6b2fbedf41a7)\nno posts folder found - the program needs its assets/posts directory beside the executable (looked in: /home/ghrunner/runner-work/Camcraft/Camcraft/target/debug/build/camcraft-post/4d4a6b2fbedf41a7/out/assets/posts)\n```\n\nEach \"looked in\" list in the logs has one path only. This includes `target/debug/assets/posts` for the uplifted `camcraft-cli`. Thus `target/debug/.fingerprint` does not exist on the runner.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`data_dir::tests::the_new_cargo_build_dir_layout_finds_the_repository_assets` (camcraft-post lib). It uses the exe paths of the runner log. It fails without the fix (`left: []`) and passes with the fix, on Windows.\n\n## Tests (Windows, cargo 1.99.0, `-j 6`, `--test-threads=6`)\n\n- `camcraft-post` lib: 76 passed (11 `data_dir` tests).\n- `camcraft-app` `shipped_from_disk`: 3 passed.\n- `camcraft-app` `golden_cl`: 33 passed.\n- `camcraft-app` `post_not_judged`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The local cargo (1.99.0) uses the old layout. I could not run a real build in the new layout on Windows. The pinning test copies the paths of the runner log, but the real layout is proved only by the next post-merge run.\n- `camcraft-motion` `corner_arc_radius` also fails on that run. It is a different defect and it fails on Windows too. It is tracked in #2317, not here.\n\nChangelog: Test executables and dev runs find the shipped posts and machine files with the new cargo build-dir layout.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2316\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
